The wiki says this is C343-415 and indicates
that it can happen in Vlad's Tower and
possibly other special levels, but it does
not explain the cause.

One supposes it can generally only
happen relatively late in the game,
because the mail daemon has a rather
higher nominal difficulty level than any
actual interaction I've had with it would
seem to justify.  (Difficulty 26 is the
same as an Archon's difficulty level.)

> and why he was just vanishing.

That's probably defensive coding.  The mail
daemon is theoretically not supposed to
appear unless it has mail for you, but if
it *does* appear with no mail to deliver,
this is what it does to resolve the situation.

The wiki also suggests that this situation
can be created artificially by re-animating
a wished-for statue.  It doesn't mention
figurines, but I wouldn't be surprised if
that can work also.  In wizard mode, it
might be possible to generate it at will
with the create monster keystroke.


